  "term": "diffusion magnetic resonance imaging",
  "definition": "Diffusion magnetic resonance imaging is an MRI-based method that assesses tissue by measuring how molecules such as water move within it. Changes in this movement, often summarized by the apparent diffusion coefficient, can reflect the tissue’s underlying microstructure.",
